# M6.1: the app requires the module but nothing imports it.
# go mod tidy drops it -> genx fails with the blank-import advice.

exec go mod download
exec go mod tidy
! exec genx
cmp stderr want/stderr.txt

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.26.0

require example.com/labels v1.0.0
-- app.go --
package app
-- genx.yaml --
version: 1

use:
  - example.com/labels: [consts]
-- want/stderr.txt --
genx: use example.com/labels: the go command can't find this package: no required module provides package example.com/labels; to add it:
	go get example.com/labels
If nothing in the app imports it yet, go mod tidy removed it from go.mod, and go mod vendor didn't copy it.
Keep a file in the app with a blank import, which the build leaves out:

	//go:build genx

	package <name>

	import _ "example.com/labels"

then run go get example.com/labels
